  "notes": "State-agency (Florida CFO) consumer-education sample declarations page -- fictional insured/carrier/policy numbers by design (a teaching sample, not a real policyholder document), but fully filled in (unlike the CMS-1500/SBA-1919/SBA-413 blank templates), so this is a genuine extraction-richness case study rather than a blank-field abstention test. deductible_hurricane is printed as '2% OF Coverage A / $3,200' -- the dollar figure is gold here since the schema field is a currency amount, not a percentage; a model extracting '2%' instead would be reading the same cell differently, worth documenting rather than silently marking wrong. Maryland Insurance Administration's declarations-page sample (also named in the original task spec) returns HTTP 403 to non-browser clients and could not be downloaded -- documented in failures.md, not substituted or faked."
